  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5cf27982398fffe4696d893c8d8f58e5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Victor - Timeline
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JusticeIsAWeapon.Data.DialogueNodeSO
  nodeId: Victor - Timeline
  speakerName: 
  lineText: "You select the 'Timeline' baseline.\r\n\r\n\r\n<b>Detective Miller:</b>
    \r\n\"Walk me through this morning. Yuki says she came to you when the door wouldn't
    open.\"\r\n\r\n<b>Victor Hasting:</b> \r\n\"She was panicked. Marcus held the
    only physical master keys, so the only way into that office once it's deadbolted
    is an emergency system override from my console. I blew the electronic lock at
    7:35 AM. We walked in, saw him on the floor, and I made the call to 911 immediately.
    Whatever happened in there, he brought on himself.\"\r\n\r\n''[Investigator's
    Note:]'' He's got the timeline down to the minute, completely validating Yuki's
    morning story. He\u2019s using his strict adherence to protocol as a shield.\r\n\r\n<b>Detective
    Miller:</b> \r\n\"Walk me through your timeline for this morning. When did you
    realize something was wrong?\"\r\n\r\n<b>Victor Hasting:</b> \r\n\"His assistant,
    Yuki, came running to my desk at 7:35 AM. She was panicking because his office
    door was deadbolted and he wasn't answering. I had to trigger an emergency system
    override from my console to blow the electronic lock. We walked in, saw him on
    the floor, and I made the call to 911 immediately. My system didn't fail; whatever
    happened in there, he brought on himself.\"\r\n\r\n''[Investigator's Note:]''
    He's got the timeline down to the minute, but he immediately involves Yuki in
    his sequence of events to validate his story. We need to verify this with her.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r"
